	quest.24C8852F25520072.quest_subtitle: "T4 / 5"
	quest.24C8852F25520072.title: "Coming Soon"
	quest.2631A613ADCD302E.quest_desc: ["Notice, try to avoid putting tools/armor/things with NBT into your stock ticker system, the stock ticker seems to have problems extracting them sometimes."]
	quest.2631A613ADCD302E.quest_subtitle: "A centralized storage"
	quest.2700DA7ED10B4664.quest_desc: [
		"Normally, gregtech spawns veins wildly all over the world at a constant fixed distance in a grid."
		""
		""
		"Frontiers has entirely discared this system for the concept of \"Ore Fields\""
		""
		""
		"Finding a field, you can expect to discover many interconnected veins of the same ore present."
		""
		"Your earliest method of finding fields is the dowsing rod, made from flint, sticks, and string."
		""
		"It will discover the nearest field to you, which you can see on your minimap/world map."
		"To find another, namely different vein, you should walk away from the field you just discovered, as there is a minimum distance between fields"
	]
	quest.2700DA7ED10B4664.quest_subtitle: "How to find resources"
	quest.2700DA7ED10B4664.title: "Ore Fields"
	quest.2928EF0DCF970AE4.quest_desc: [
		"Fans are extremely powerful in base create."
		""
		"You can wash composite ore with a Create fan to bulk-sift for tiny-dusts from ores if you wish to not manually sift every stack of ore you crush."
		""
		"&cSmelting/Smoking abilities have been disabled&r, as Create fans allow abnormally powerful processing capabilities compared to most if not all GT multis."
		""
		"This was the compromise for letting them be used for literally everything else (including aircraft) instead of gating them to Mid MV like before."
	]
	quest.2928EF0DCF970AE4.quest_subtitle: "A note about Fans."
	quest.2AA6F78DB2ED60F2.quest_desc: [
		" &7&oYou have dreamed."
		""
		" &7&oA world that was yours, the way you wanted it to be, without flaw, "
		" &7&ogiven your full love"
		""
		" &7&oAlas, this world you made is not for you, it is for the future you have lost.&r"
		""
		" &7&oAwaken."
		""
		""
		" &o&cERROR &7- Inducing Temporal Amnesia has failed.&r"
	]
	quest.2AA6F78DB2ED60F2.quest_subtitle: "We all start somewhere"
	quest.2AA6F78DB2ED60F2.title: "Gather Some Wood"
	quest.2ABEE21EB889B7DD.quest_desc: [
		"Did you know you can throw iron ingots and coal/charcoal dust into lava to batch craft wrought iron?"
		""
		"Give it a try! Wrought Iron is wonderful for early tools!"
	]
	quest.2ABEE21EB889B7DD.quest_subtitle: "Easier Wrought Iron"
	quest.31B6D09FBE2173EF.quest_desc: [
		"Get down near the bedrock layer and place an ember bore ontop of bedrock, with a mechanical core on the center block, insert coal (or other fuels, haven't tried) into the mechanical core with your logistics of choice (hopper will do). The bore will start to run and produce ember as long as there is ember available for extraction in the chunk"
		""
		""
		"Before you find a place for your bore, you should make an atmospheric gauge, the more the dial increases, the more ember there is"
	]
	quest.31B6D09FBE2173EF.quest_subtitle: "Gathering your First Ember"
	quest.32CBFA838C794C01.quest_desc: ["Allows you to build rituals easier, and that will help in the future."]
	quest.32CBFA838C794C01.quest_subtitle: "Something you might want"
	quest.35B7A194BB34BA44.quest_desc: [
		"The \"&6Weirdly Durable Hammer&r\" has infinite durability and can mine obsidian."
		""
		"Like all other tools, it can be buffed massively by enchanting it with efficiency."
		"This is an Optional Quest."
		""
		" &o&#A3A3A3A world stretches before you, wealthy in infinite resources."
		" &o&#A3A3A3Your humble hands struggle to extract enough materials alone."
		" &o&#A3A3A3And thus, whispers remind you of an old lost friend."
		" &o&#A3A3A3And once again, you carve through the world like paper."
	]
	quest.35B7A194BB34BA44.quest_subtitle: "The unsual that is willed to be. "
	quest.35B7A194BB34BA44.title: "An Indestructable Ally"
	quest.3733906CF47B1C06.quest_subtitle: "Multipurpose and cheap"
	quest.38473AAE9EFA91C7.quest_desc: [
		"Ember is easy to move!"
		""
		"Just place an Ember Emitter onto your source of embers, and connected it to an ember receptor with a tinker hammer."
	]
	quest.38473AAE9EFA91C7.quest_subtitle: "Moving Ember"
	quest.3945947DBE1D85A0.quest_subtitle: "Tier 3 Overworld Resources"
	quest.3A755F7B8012AB1A.quest_subtitle: "Create Oxygen Tank"
	quest.3E42DDEBA9DBB13C.quest_desc: [
		"The second layer of the abyss seems to be populated more densely with biomass than the first layer."
		""
		"This indicates the first layer is notably some kind of &nfeeding ground&r for a large organism or many smaller organisms."
		""
		"I would assume the Murkbloom consumes biomass at the surface and then sinks back down to deeper layers and &9provides nutrients to the rockbed&r."
		""
		"I should be careful, my passive sonars are detecting &6unusual spikes of activity in the water&r. It's safe to assume the density of Murkbloom here is higher, and more agressive to the sounds I make."
		""
		"I should consider researching the plantlife within the first layer of the Hollowed Abyss, they may allow me to mimic their sound supressing biology."
	]
	quest.3E42DDEBA9DBB13C.quest_subtitle: "Biodiversity in the fog. (Y-200 to Y-400)"
	quest.3E42DDEBA9DBB13C.title: "The Hollow Abyss - Layer 2 : Muted Shelves"
	quest.3FB852AA4A2FBB8B.quest_desc: [
		"Primitive Pumps allow passive collection of water."
		""
		""
		"If you haven't i'd recommend making one to automatically fill your boilers before you start!"
	]
	quest.3FB852AA4A2FBB8B.quest_subtitle: "Did you make a pump?"
	quest.448F8668DD3AEB72.quest_desc: [
		"As you've been playing, you most likely noticed many foods have a stat on them that says something like..."
		""
		"&e\"Main Course\""
		"&e\"Side\""
		"&e\"Drink\""
		""
		""
		"These are the 3 Food Classifications that exist for &ocreating meals&r, and all meals start with a &emain course&r."
		""
		"Right click your main course of choice onto the hearth plate, and optionally add a side and drink."
		"When you are ready. Eat your food by &nright clicking&r. Your meal will become a great memory!"
		""
		"You may have 1 memorized meal active at a time, and it will last until you die or eat another meal. You will get the combined stats of the entire meal as a permanent buff until then. (A way to see the combined buff will be in a future UI addition, most likely hovering over the icon itself)"
		""
		""
		"Eating a variety of meals increases your taste profile, the more unique meals you've consumed oveer time, the stronger the impact of meals becomes. New meals only get added to your taste profile once per minecraft day, so you can only improve this by trying meals often."
		""
		"Eating the same meal over and over will eventually make it a \"Signature Meal\", which will prompt the player to shift-right-click their empty plate after a qualifiying meal, Signature meals are permanent and will grant you a portion of their stats forever, even after dying."
		""
		"&6"
		"UIs for tracking your pallete/taste profile and Signature meals will come in a future update along with another system which can house their GUI elements.&r"
	]
	quest.448F8668DD3AEB72.quest_subtitle: "A meal to remember"
	quest.469D5D2740B79048.quest_desc: [
		"The powderizer will convert purified ores into a finely ground dust for chemical sepperation."
		""
		"Sorting the ground dust will give you the same outputs as regular purified ore sorting does."
		""
		"So make sure you run it through flotation again!"
	]
	quest.469D5D2740B79048.quest_subtitle: "Finely Ground (Tier 2 Ore Processing)"
	quest.46A8D660ABEB83FA.quest_desc: [
		"&eBronze&r is useful for crafting rudimentary frames and parts for machines."
		""
		""
		"The earliest method you have is using a &6mortar&r to shred your copper ingots and tin nuggets into dust, and then crafting those into bronze."
		""
		"Once you have access to a &6compressor&r and &6alloy smelter&r, you can make bronze much more efficiently."
		""
		""
		""
		""
		"You will need a LOT of bronze, gather as much copper as you can."
		"I'd recommend finding a trial chamber and scrapping the copper from it. "
		"...or an Cuprosiva Ore Field."
	]
	quest.46A8D660ABEB83FA.quest_subtitle: "The First Alloy"
	quest.4A90C6B25FC79EAC.quest_desc: [
		"Stick this down, hopper ember shards/crystals in, watch it turn into ember"
		""
		"use the tinkers hammer on ember emitters/receptors to link them together."
	]
	quest.4A90C6B25FC79EAC.quest_subtitle: "Activating Ember"
	quest.4C8AB307C45DBC3C.quest_subtitle: "Content Blocker"
	quest.4C8AB307C45DBC3C.title: "Below Hell, The Undergarden"
	quest.4CBACE925D480CAA.quest_desc: [
		"When entering the deepslate level of the world, the air will become too thin to breathe normally."
		""
		"To aide in this, you can craft several items that counter air loss"
		""
		"Rebreather : Will double your air-capacity in thin-air environments"
		""
		"Reinforced Rebreather : Will halt oxygen loss in thin air and no air environments as long as you have a valid Oxygen Supply Tank (Bronze or Steel) "
		""
		"Create Backtank : Also compatible with the Reinforced Rebreather for pre-oxygen usage."
		""
		""
		""
		"For environments inside of water, you will have to use a Diving Helmet + Tanks of your choice."
		"This might not work/apply in all cases, please let me know if you find strange places you can/can't breathe when you should/shouldn't be able to!"
	]
	quest.4CBACE925D480CAA.quest_subtitle: "Breathing in places you can't"
	quest.50930E8761259EFD.quest_desc: [
		"It says parallel, but it's more like 'batch processing'"
		""
		""
		"the more dense and faster the recipe, the better return per ingot of steel is"
		""
		""
		"Best combo (Wrought Iron Block + Coke Block) will result in about a 50% duration cut per steel ingot!"
	]
	quest.50930E8761259EFD.quest_subtitle: "The tooltip lies"
	quest.50A60E8F488274DF.quest_subtitle: "Flocculation Solution"
	quest.534DBCED4E339D89.quest_desc: [
		"Stick an Ember receptor on it, and an ember emitter on your ember source."
		""
		"Use the Tinkering Hammer to connect them."
		""
		""
		"This is a pretty temporary recipe until i can be asked to make Steam Ember Hatches."
	]
	quest.534DBCED4E339D89.quest_subtitle: "Getting Embers into a Gregtech Machine"
	quest.547989FC1806F95F.quest_desc: [
		"You can get these ore chunks by first washing your crushed ore in a flotation plant."
		""
		"After which you then run through an ore sorter to get the chunks, these chunks can be processed into their respective materials"
		""
		""
		"First Sources of : "
		""
		"Aluminium (From Saphire dust elecytrolysis)"
		"Bauxite (For Titanium in the Future)"
	]
	quest.547989FC1806F95F.title: "Tier 1 Overworld Resources"
	quest.5505401B1E8344EB.quest_subtitle: "The Key to Steel"
	quest.57E59B0060EAB2C7.quest_desc: [
		"Welcome to Cosmic Frontiers, we're glad to have you here."
		""
		"This quest is to get some housekeeping and information out of the way that's important to remember while playing Frontiers."
		""
		"1. &6We heavily modify the content of many mods, to the point that bug reports should not be submitted to mod devs. Please report &lALL&r &6issues to the modpack Github Firstly.&r"
		"Reporting issues/crashes from this pack to mod devs may waste their time on mechanics that are pack exclusive and aren't relevant anywhere else."
		""
		"&bModpack Github&r : https://github.com/Frontiers-PackForge/CosmicFrontiers/issues"
		"&bModpack Discord&r : https://discord.com/invite/fkxPAq9VQp"
		""
		"2. &eThis modpack has a built in narrative and story, quest chapters automatically appear when you reach major goals in the previous chapter.&r"
		"&4&lBE WARNED: Enabling Edit Mode in the questbook may spoil the suprise."
		""
		"3. When you are ready to begin, head over to the Steam Age Chapter"
		""
		"Dev Note :"
		"&aThe pack is currently in active development, and has recently migrated to 1.21."
		"&aQuestbook will be improved as development goes along!&r"
		"&aCore Mechanics and descriptions of them will be added here in time."
	]
	quest.57E59B0060EAB2C7.quest_subtitle: "Welcome to Frontiers"
	quest.57E59B0060EAB2C7.title: "Welcome to Cosmic Frontiers"
	quest.5973534E85F5D126.quest_subtitle: "Better Iesnium"
	quest.5B91A99F1F8B588D.quest_subtitle: "Oh hey, brass!"
	quest.601F4BCD183CC077.quest_subtitle: "A mundane but durable metal"
	quest.67110A5418804D33.quest_desc: [
		"You can't harvest pure nether quartz yourself, and gold is something only found in small amounts now."
		""
		""
		"I suggest you either raid bastions and trade with piglins, villagers, or consider getting to LV :^)"
	]
	quest.67110A5418804D33.quest_subtitle: "Piglin Economics 101"
	quest.687032030F774208.title: "Breathing in the Abyss"
	quest.6E3EDA485D3AD5F7.quest_desc: [
		"In the waters of the undergarden you have discovered a strange, lightless chasm into the depths."
		""
		"The water rumbles as if it's alive and waiting for something."
		""
		"The topmost layer seeems to be mostly empty, with some landmasses poking up above what seems to be a thick fog."
		""
		"This fog threshold seems to be either holding something back, or keeping something out."
		""
		"Before Leaving, I heard some sort of clicking sound, aimed at me."
		"Something else is waiting for me down there."
	]
	quest.6E3EDA485D3AD5F7.quest_subtitle: "The only way forward, is down. (Y-64 to Y-200)"
	quest.6E3EDA485D3AD5F7.title: "The Hollow Abyss - Layer 1 : The Shaded Sea"
	quest.6E8D634B042DB26F.quest_desc: [
		""
		""
		"Across the hot and cold regions of this world seem to be plants that aid in thermal managment."
		""
		"Sun ferns spawn in &6hot biomes&r and help you with &bcold&r via &6heating coating&r"
		""
		"Ice ferns spawn in &bcold biomes&r and help you with &6heat&r via &bcooling coating&r"
		""
		"You can gain the combined benefit of both coatings by making &5Thermal Coating&r."
	]
	quest.6E8D634B042DB26F.quest_subtitle: "The Weather and You"
	quest.6E8D634B042DB26F.title: "Thermal Woes"
	quest.6ED6791358655950.quest_desc: ["Holds as much stuff as a double chest in one block, awesome!"]
	quest.6ED6791358655950.quest_subtitle: "Better Storage"
	quest.6EF94519E4BCBE72.quest_desc: [
		"Occultism Got updated..."
		""
		""
		"Packdev doesn't know the new content. please hold while i learn it lol"
	]
	quest.6EF94519E4BCBE72.quest_subtitle: "Soooo"
	quest.70C78D038EBF6CA6.quest_desc: [
		"Rock Cutting wheels will cleave large areas of material away when active."
		""
		"Their SU cost scales with size. it's generally recommended to make many small blades vs 1 large one."
		""
		""
		"These are useful, strictly because you can automate mining with massive airships if you are so inclined. and attaching huge harvester arms to simulated contraptions for early game mining really changes how you play."
	]
	quest.70C78D038EBF6CA6.quest_subtitle: "Mass Contraption Mining"
	quest.725672ED730CE824.quest_desc: [
		"creosote grease can act as a fill in for honeycomb in a few recipes."
		""
		"it requires a lot more than honeycomb, however"
	]
	quest.725672ED730CE824.quest_subtitle: "A saving grace - Alternate to Honey"
	quest.72A429BEF13F8845.quest_desc: [
		"You can attune it to netherrack to scan for iesnium in the nether."
		""
		""
		""
		"If you have an AMD graphics card, you will need to modify the Occultism config file to enable AMD compatibility"
	]
	quest.72A429BEF13F8845.quest_subtitle: "Click Netherack"
	quest.733582199AB1E7B7.quest_subtitle: "Find some bees"
	quest.7A016FB22E827915.quest_desc: [
		"Diving below the heavy fog, the clicking seems to be more of a faint but persisting chittering."
		""
		"Something is moving through all of the water around me, some kind of &#9B3F9Dpathogen bloom&r, large dark masses of it float around."
		""
		"Off in the distance, I see a Gloomper Toad sink below the fog, out in the open water."
		""
		"In less than &#FF050A15 seconds&r the entire water turned into a chorus of clicking, chittering, and what I can only describe as a grotesque gurgling sound as the &#FF0505entire creature was dissolved whole&r."
		""
		"I will name this phenomena, \"&#D203E5The Murkbloom&r\", It is within my best interest that I stay as quiet, if not more quiet, as I would if dealing with a Warden."
		""
		"Something tells me I should &cavoid open water as often as possible&r, and listen to my surroundings &nvery closely&r"
		""
		"I tried to establish a warp point near the abyss, to find that this place is the source of &dAnti-magic emissions&r I've been dealing with. Seems Teleporting into the depths will be impossible for now."
		""
		"If I dive &cdeep enough&r, I might discover how to get my &aspell book&r working again."
	]
	quest.7A016FB22E827915.quest_subtitle: "Silence is the standard."
	quest.7A016FB22E827915.title: "An Unseen Threat: The Murkbloom"
	quest.7BAA63BF7EE181C3.quest_desc: [
		"Cuprosiva ore is one of the many Composite Ores that exist across the overworld."
		""
		""
		""
		"All Composite ore is truly 6 seperate ore types in one ore! you'll eventually learn to seperate the ore in increasingly complex sorting steps."
		""
		""
		"For now, you can directly smelt curposiva for copper."
		""
		"You can get &6Tin Nuggets&r by \"Manually Sorting\" Cuprosiva, hold right click on Crushed Cuprosiva to find some tin nuggets."
		""
		"Also worth noting, you can do this to Fersosine as well to get gold nuggets"
	]
